{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ada8-0185-76f0-8192-f6e1be48611d"},"sequence":5,"recorded_at":1780531400000005,"record_type":"status","durability":"ephemeral","causation_id":"e58530cc-c434-4c84-a6d6-35c15a8ccfca","payload_type":"turn.input.user","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"turn_input_user","command_id":"e58530cc-c434-4c84-a6d6-35c15a8ccfca","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e58530cc-c434-4c84-a6d6-35c15a8ccfca"},"prompt":"# Agent Task Assignment\n\n## FIRST — Run Immediately\n\n```bash\ntask-board m 'set_status(TASK-260909-2ez769, status=reviewing)'\n```\n\n## Operational Constraints (Headless Run)\n\n- Never background a long command and end your turn: a headless session ends with\n  the turn and the process dies with it, while the run is still recorded as\n  completed with no evidence attached.\n- A single shell call is time-bounded (~10 minutes). Split long checks into\n  bounded sequential calls (package subsets, `-run` masks) and state explicitly\n  what you reran yourself versus accepted from already-attached evidence.\n- Attach evidence before you end the lifecycle, not after: \"I will attach it when\n  the run finishes\" is unfulfillable by construction.\n\nRun `task-board spawn directives \"$TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID\"` at safe checkpoints,\nat most once per 1 minute, never in a loop.\nDirectives have no delivery timer.\nSave before cancel; pause/reroute safely.\nIf reading directives fails, report unknown; do not treat it as none.\n\n\n## Role Contract\n\n- **Role:** `reviewer` (`reviewer`) — Reviews implementation quality and project fit\n- Obey task scope, acceptance criteria, and checklist.\n- Report real exit codes; failing gates stay failing.\n- Use scoped board projections; skip `summary()`,\n  `plan()`, `schema()`, and `{ full }`. Request scoped schema only after an\n  unknown call.\n- Load only relevant and explicitly required skills.\n\n### Skills\n\n- `project-management`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/SKILL.md`\n- `architecture-diagrams`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/architecture-diagrams/SKILL.md`\n\n### Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Preserve and verify all foreign RPC bytes and checkpointed SSH/peer work; isolate only enumerated RPC delta and use managed current-base transition before credentials implementation.\n- [ ] Implement exact closed Config4 and Host Trust Store readers; refuse missing, partial, unreadable, ambiguous or downgraded state without implicit legacy fallback.\n- [ ] Implement explicit out-of-band enrollment, unique credential-to-host mapping, fresh-key bounded rotation, immediate revocation and current-generation mutation authorization through production APIs.\n- [ ] Provide owner-only credential custody and atomic crash-durable trust writes, with platform custody and crash/recovery evidence and no secret replication.\n- [ ] Implement exact-preview confirmed Config4 migration, complete peer enrollment, durable apply and rollback while preserving accepted Config1/2/3 and SSH/peer behavior.\n- [ ] Demonstrate complete pinned v0.6.0 sections 6.6 and 11.10.2/3 acceptance through positive and narrowing-negative production tests; preserve truthful mutation controls and exact-source results; pass required local checks.\n- [ ] Code written per task description and AC\n- [ ] Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\n- [ ] In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n- [ ] Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows