{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c615","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ada8-0185-76f0-8192-f6e1be48611d"},"sequence":357,"recorded_at":1780531400000709,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e58530cc-c434-4c84-a6d6-35c15a8ccfca","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e58530cc-c434-4c84-a6d6-35c15a8ccfca","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e58530cc-c434-4c84-a6d6-35c15a8ccfca"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ada8-a0fb-7ea3-b5d6-2cebce5956e3"},"task_id":"01a0ada8-a0fb-7ea3-b5d6-2cebce5956e3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ada8-a0fb-7ea3-b5d6-2cebce5956e3","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev12/TASK-260909-2ez769_results-rev12.md`.\n1|# TASK-260909-2ez769 rev12 outcome — call-site census + side-effect-free binding refusal\n2|\n3|Producer: RUN-260917-39ee2b (muse-spark max), continuing the partial\n4|rev12 candidate of RUN-260917-b6de1b (codex, killed by provider quota\n5|before publishing; no candidate bytes discarded).\n6|\n7|Base: managed `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` advanced the\n8|Story worktree to protected trunk `62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e`,\n9|replaying the checkpointed peer/SSH leaves as `efe119a`/`5e54874`\n10|(signatures verify). Candidate branch head `5e54874`, worktree\n11|UNCOMMITTED. Candidate delta: 74 paths (17 tracked modifications +\n12|57 untracked additions; the CR11 `__pycache__` bytecode is removed and\n13|`internal/hosttrust/binding_rebind_test.go` is added).\n14|\n15|## CR11 findings repaired\n16|\n17|F1 (call-site admission): `writepath_census_types_test.go` now admits\n18|an interface/type-parameter edge only for the exact `*types.Func`\n19|object at an exact inventoried source site (file/line/column), with\n20|top-level fail-fast hold-guard dominance for the four pair writers\n21|(`replaceDurably`, `writeTempReplace`, `commitDocument`,\n22|`commitConfigBinding`). The 119-site inventory is enumerated with\n23|per-group production justifications in\n24|`TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev12.md`. The committed\n25|regression `TestWritePathCensusRejectsUnlistedInterfaceCallSite` ports\n26|the CR11 `reviewer_callsite_test.go` probe and extends it: plants\n27|before AND after `requireHoldForConfig` must both rename real files\n28|in the child witness (PASS) while the child census refuses both\n29|unlisted sites (FAIL). The narrowing mutant\n30|`writepath-interface-callsite-skip` preserves method identity while\n31|dropping site/hold admission and is killed by that regression. The\n32|former method-spelling interface admission predicate is removed;\n33|remaining name-keyed maps are fail-closed concrete-call detectors\n34|only (claim narrowed in the census doc). The 17 standalone CR11\n35|plants remain killed.\n36|\n37|F2 (refused rebind claims a target): `ensureConfigBindingLocked`\n38|validates the existing store-side association and the target-side\n39|association under the bootstrap lock BEFORE publishing either side; a\n40|refused request leaves both the existing association and the\n41|previously unclaimed target untouched. Committed RED-first regression\n42|`TestReviewerRefusedRebindLeavesTargetUnclaimed` (RED log:\n43|`rebind-red-rev12.log`), plus\n44|`TestCompetingFirstBindingsPublishExactlyOneAssociation` (two handles\n45|opened before binding; exactly one winner, loser side-effect free)\n46|and `TestInterruptedFirstBindingIsRepairedAfterReopen` (target\n47|durable + index missing is repaired on reopen; target never rebound).\n48|The CR11 second-pair foreign-root refusal still holds.\n49|\n50|Hygiene: no `__pycache__`/`.pyc` under `internal/`; all Python runs\n51|with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; README tool row describes the\n52|all-indirect-call policy and its exact exceptions; evidence attached\n53|as real binaries (verified below).\n54|\n55|## AC coverage: 19 of 21 rows driven (rows 15, 21 stated bounds)\n56|\n57|| # | Acceptance row | Production call / named test evidence | Result |\n58||---:|---|---|---|\n59|| 1 | Closed Config4 | `config.Decode`; `TestDecodeConfiguration4Refusals` | pass |\n60|| 2 | Historical compatibility + explicit migration | `config.Migrate`/legacy migration; `TestMigrateRefusesV4Target`, `TestMigrateRefusesV4Downgrade`, `TestLegacyMigrateCannotOverwriteCommittedV4`, `TestLegacyMigrateConvergesUnreplacedMarkerThenCommits`, `TestLegacyMigrateRefusesAfterReplacementLanded` | pass |\n61|| 3 | Closed trust document | `hosttrust.DecodeTrust`; `TestDecodeTrustRefusals` | pass |\n62|| 4 | Missing/corrupt/unreadable trust | `hosttrust.ReadSnapshot`; `TestReadSnapshotMissingStore`, `TestCorruptTrustRefusedNeverEmpty`, `TestReadSnapshotRefusesUnreadableMarker` | pass |\n63|| 5 | Fresh issuance | `hosttrust.IssueCredential`; `TestIssueCredentialProfile`, `TestIssueSelfEnrollsActive` | pass |\n64|| 6 | Exact profile + time bounds | `hosttrust.VerifyProfile`; `TestVerifyProfileRefusals`, `TestVerifyProfileRefusesJustPastExpiry`, wrong-key-usage/EKU/SAN tests | pass |\n65|| 7 | Explicit tuple enrollment | `hosttrust.Store.Enroll`; `TestEnrollRefusals`, `TestEnrollBoundsPerHost`; OOB human verification remains an operator act | pass within stated OOB boundary |\n66|| 8 | Mapping uniqueness | `hosttrust.DecodeTrust` + admission; duplicate credential/root/key/digest cases in `TestDecodeTrustRefusals`, `TestEnrollBoundsPerHost`, lifecycle tests | pass |\n67|| 9 | Rotation/retirement bounds | `hosttrust.Rotate`, `MarkRetiring`; `TestRotateBoundedWindow`, `TestRotateCapsAtLeafExpiry`, `TestMarkRetiringCapsAtLeafExpiry` | pass |\n68|| 10 | Revocation tombstones | `hosttrust.Revoke`, `Enroll`; `TestRevokeTombstone`, `TestRevokedLeafNeverReenrolls`, `TestRevocationClosesAuthorization` | pass |\n69|| 11 | Old-generation mutation refusal | `hosttrust.WithMutationAuthorization`; `TestWithMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleGeneration`, `TestMutationAuthorizationRefusesStaleAfterConvergence` | pass |\n70|| 12 | Shared authorization serialization | `hosttrust.Open`/lock, `WithMutationAuthorization`, `Revoke`; `TestFirstOpenPreservesHeldLock`, `TestConcurrentOpenAttachesToExistingLock`, `TestMutationAuthorizationSerializesWithRevocation`, `TestMutationAuthorizationSerializesWithSeparateStoreRevocation`; binding precondition `Store.EnsureConfigBinding` + `TestReviewerRefusedRebindLeavesTargetUnclaimed`, `TestCompetingFirstBindingsPublishExactlyOneAssociation`, `TestInterruptedFirstBindingIsRepairedAfterReopen` (rev12) | pass |\n71|| 13 | Coherent config+trust snapshot | `config.LoadCoherent`; `TestSurvivingReaderConvergesInterruptedApply`, `TestSurvivingReaderConvergesInterruptedRollback`, `TestSurvivingReaderRefusesDivergedConfig`, barrier and revalidation tests | pass |\n72|| 14 | Unix owner custody | `hosttrust.Open`, `ValidateCustody`; `TestCustodyRefusals`, `TestValidateCustodyBindsDirectory`, `TestOpenCreatesOwnerOnlyLayout` | pass on Darwin |\n73|| 15 | Windows equivalent ACLs | `verifyOwner`, `installOwnerOnlyACL`, `secureStaged`; `custody_windows_test.go` seven native tests | stated bound: no Windows runtime runner; cross-build, test-compile, and vet pass |\n74|| 16 | Complete peers + selected credential | `config.PreviewV4`; `TestPreviewV4PeerEnrollment`, `TestPreviewV4CredentialGates` | pass |\n75|| 17 | Exact preview + confirmation | `config.ApplyV4`; `TestApplyV4PreviewMismatch`, `TestApplyV4ConfirmRequiredWithDrops`; write discipline `TestWritePathCensusRejectsUnlistedInterfaceCallSite` (rev12) | pass |\n76|| 18 | Current source/generation apply | Config4 apply + `hosttrust.JointCommit`; `TestApplyV4StaleSource`, `TestApplyV4StaleGeneration`, revalidation and stale-marker tests | pass |\n77|| 19 | Crash-durable config/trust pair | Config4 apply/rollback + `hosttrust.JointCommit`, `Recover`, convergence; `TestApplyV4CrashConvergesGeneration`, surviving-reader/barrier/compensation tests | pass |\n78|| 20 | Explicit backup rollback | `config.RollbackV4`; `TestRollbackV4*`, `TestPublishedBackupNamesStayExcluded`, `TestApplyV4BackupIsClassifiedConfigCopy` | pass |\n79|| 21 | Secret exclusion across export surfaces | `hosttrust.MatchExcludedFromReplication`, `ExcludedConfigDirName`; matcher and persisted handoff/owner-note evidence | stated bound: repository matcher only; downstream consumers and diagnostics are unowned |\n80|\n81|Rows 15/21 are NOT DRIVEN. No post-lock-release dispatch, mesh-wide\n82|revocation, physical power-loss, or authenticated-human verification\n83|guarantee is inferred. RPC transport/admission remains outside this leaf.\n84|\n85|## Mutation batteries (exact final source, per-plant raw logs)\n86|\n87|Reran in full on the post-refresh final tree with\n88|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` (4 parallel streams, 9 bounded groups,\n89|exits from subprocess return codes; per-mutant overlay, `test.log`,\n90|`results.json`, `table.md` under\n91|`.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/mutations-{config,hosttrust}-rev12post-groupN`,\n92|also archived in the evidence tarball):\n93|\n94|- Config4 (`internal/config/mutations_v4.py`): 1 neutral control\n95|  passed (exit 0) + 13 narrowing/precision mutants killed (exit 1\n96|  with the expected named test failing), 0 survivors. Includes the\n97|  new `writepath-interface-callsite-skip` (killed by\n98|  `TestWritePathCensusRejectsUnlistedInterfaceCallSite`),\n99|  `writepath-method-value-skip`, and `config-association-root-skip`.\n100|- Host Trust Store (`internal/hosttrust/mutations.py`): 1 neutral\n101|  control passed (exit 0) + 34 narrowing/precision mutants killed\n102|  (exit 1 with the expected named test failing), 0 survivors.\n103|  Includes `hold-state-root-skip` (killed by\n104|  `TestHeldExclusiveRejectsForeignConfigStateRoot`) and the\n105|  preserve-token `compensate-verify-before-restore` order swap\n106|  (behavioral suite kill).\n107|- Aggregate: 47 killed, 2 neutrals passed, 0 survivors; every kill\n108|  verified from `results.json` (exit 1 + expected test in failing\n109|  set).\n110|\n111|## Local validation (exact final source)\n112|\n113|- `gofmt -l` (repo, excluding `.temp`/`.task-board`): clean.\n114|- `go vet ./...` (native): exit 0.\n115|- `go mod tidy -diff`: exit 0 (offline, `GOFLAGS=-mod=mod`).\n116|- `git diff --check`: clean (excluding board checkout noise).\n117|- `go build ./...`: exit 0 native, darwin/arm64, linux/arm64, windows/amd64.\n118|- `go test ./... -count=1`: exit 0, all packages ok (see `go-test-all-rev12post.log`).\n119|- Coverage (`-count=1 -cover`): config 92.9%, hosttrust 76.3%,\n120|  peeridentity 97.5%, secprim 94.4%, localstore 83.8% — exit 0.\n121|- Windows test compilation (`-exec /usr/bin/true -run '^$'`) and\n122|  `GOOS=windows go vet` on config+hosttrust: exit 0 (no Windows\n123|  runtime claim; stated bound row 15).\n124|- `-race` on hosttrust+config: exit 0.\n125|- Key verbose runs: `TestWritePathCensusGate` +\n126|  `TestWritePathCensusRejectsUnlistedInterfaceCallSite` pass\n127|  (11.99s); F2 trio passes (0.81s).\n128|  (`census-regression-rev12post.log`, `binding-tests-rev12post.log`).\n129|- Independent RED: the F2 trio against unfixed CR11 code fails with\n130|  exit 1 on `TestReviewerRefusedRebindLeavesTargetUnclaimed`\n131|  (`rebind-red-rev12post.log`); adjacent pins pass pre/post fix.\n132|- Pinned spec: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md` sha256 matches\n133|  `internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json` (`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`).\n134|\n135|## Preservation\n136|\n137|- RPC backup manifest 15/15 and parked delta 11/11 sha256 match\n138|  (`preservation-rev12post.log`).\n139|- Candidate delta 74 paths; literal RPC-manifest overlap is README.md\n140|  only (documented host-credentials/Config4/tooling section; original\n141|  RPC README bytes preserved in backup). No RPC implementation path\n142|  absorbed.\n143|- SSH/peer checkpoint directories byte-identical across the replay;\n144|  `internal/peeridentity/v4_interop_test.go` is this leaf's only\n145|  peeridentity path.\n146|- Replayed checkpoints `efe119a`/`5e54874` verify against the\n147|  configured author key.\n148|\n149|## Bounds restated\n150|\n151|Native Windows ACL runtime execution and downstream\n152|replication/diagnostic consumers are explicit bounds, not passes. The\n153|census executes for the active Go build context. No claim covers\n154|dispatch after shared-lock release or Windows DACL runtime\n155|validation beyond cross-compilation.\n156|\n157|## Handoff\n158|\n159|Ready for review. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no\n160|main push or integration performed. Independent review follows.","final_result":true}}}
