:12 | no | Owner-only mode enforcement on the staged file. |\n72|| writeTempFile | migrationFile.Sync | migration.go 484:12 | no | File fsync before the atomic rename. |\n73|| rollbackV4 | migrationFileSystem.ReadFile | migration_v4_apply.go 212:22 | no | Read of backup/source bytes during explicit rollback. |\n74|| writeTempReplace | migrationFileSystem.Rename | migration_v4_helpers.go 137:12 | yes | Atomic install of the staged replacement bytes. |\n75|| writeTempReplace | migrationFileSystem.Remove | migration_v4_helpers.go 138:7 | yes | Staging cleanup when the install does not proceed. |\n76|| restorePresentEmptyMaps | reflect.Type.Kind | schema.go 558:38 | no | Closed-shape map restoration; pure reflection, no I/O. |\n77|| restorePresentEmptyMaps | reflect.Type.Key | schema.go 558:38, 567:65 | no | Closed-shape map restoration; pure reflection, no I/O. |\n78|| restorePresentEmptyMaps | reflect.Type.Field | schema.go 562:17 | no | Closed-shape map restoration; pure reflection, no I/O. |\n79|| validateTerminal | BackendSettingsValidator.ValidateBackendSettings | validation.go 849:13 | no | Registered backend-settings validator callback. |\n80|\n81|### internal/hosttrust\n82|\n83|| Function | Edge | Sites | Hold | Production justification |\n84||---|---|---|---|---|\n85|| (AuthRequest).Format | fmt.State.Write | authorize.go 35:9 | no | Redacted `%v` formatting; no filesystem I/O. |\n86|| (Snapshot).Format | fmt.State.Write | authorize.go 42:9 | no | Redacted `%v` formatting; no filesystem I/O. |\n87|| readCommitted | FileSystem.Lstat | authorize.go 89:15 | no | Existence probe for the committed trust document. |\n88|| readCommitted | FileSystem.ReadFile | authorize.go 96:19 | no | Owner-only read of the committed trust document. |\n89|| (Store).commitConfigBinding | FileSystem.CreateTemp | binding.go 319:17 | yes | Staged authoritative target-side binding record. |\n90|| (Store).commitConfigBinding | StagedFile.Name | binding.go 323:10 | yes | Staged binding name for the atomic rename. |\n91|| (Store).commitConfigBinding | StagedFile.Sync | binding.go 329:12 | yes | Binding fsync before the atomic rename. |\n92|| (Store).commitConfigBinding | StagedFile.Close | binding.go 330:7, 333:12 | yes | Staged handle close on error and success paths. |\n93|| (Store).commitConfigBinding | FileSystem.Chmod | binding.go 336:12 | yes | Owner-only mode enforcement on the staged binding. |\n94|| (Store).commitConfigBinding | FileSystem.Rename | binding.go 342:12 | yes | Atomic publish of the authoritative binding record. |\n95|| loadBindingAt | FileSystem.Lstat | binding.go 146:15 | no | Existence probe for a binding document. |\n96|| loadBindingAt | FileSystem.ReadFile | binding.go 156:19 | no | Owner-only read of a binding document. |\n97|| ensureOwnerDir | FileSystem.Lstat | custody.go 269:15, 292:14 | no | Directory existence/kind probes during custody setup. |\n98|| ensureOwnerDir | FileSystem.MkdirAll | custody.go 278:12 | no | Owner-only directory creation during store setup. |\n99|| ensureOwnerDir | FileSystem.Chmod | custody.go 283:12 | no | Owner-only mode enforcement on the store directory. |\n100|| verifyLockFile | FileSystem.Lstat | custody.go 334:16 | no | Lock-file probe during custody verification. |\n101|| verifyLockFile | io/fs.FileInfo.Mode | custody.go 338:7, 338:34 | no | Lock-file mode verification; no writes. |\n102|| verifyOwnerDir | io/fs.FileInfo.IsDir | custody.go 300:6 | no | Directory-kind verification; no writes. |\n103|| verifyOwnerDir | io/fs.FileInfo.Mode | custody.go 303:5 | no | Directory-mode verification; no writes. |\n104|| verifyOwnerFile | io/fs.FileInfo.Mode | custody.go 351:6, 354:5 | no | File-mode verification; no writes. |\n105|| platformModeOK | io/fs.FileInfo.Mode | custody_unix.go 15:9 | no | Unix mode comparison; no writes. |\n106|| verifyOwner | io/fs.FileInfo.Sys | custody_unix.go 26:14 | no | Owner-identity extraction; no writes. |\n107|| cleanupCredentialDirectory | FileSystem.Remove | enroll.go 206:6, 207:6, 208:6, 209:6 | no | Removal of partially staged credential files after a failed enroll. |\n108|| readOwnerFile | FileSystem.Lstat | enroll.go 272:15 | no | Credential-file probe. |\n109|| readOwnerFile | FileSystem.ReadFile | enroll.go 279:19 | no | Owner-only credential-file read. |\n110|| writeCustodyFile | FileSystem.CreateTemp | enroll.go 162:17 | no | Staged credential-file creation. |\n111|| writeCustodyFile | StagedFile.Name | enroll.go 166:13 | no | Staged credential name for the atomic rename. |\n112|| writeCustodyFile | StagedFile.Close | enroll.go 170:7, 177:7, 181:7, 184:12 | no | Staged handle close on each outcome path. |\n113|| writeCustodyFile | FileSystem.Remove | enroll.go 171:7 | no | Staged credential cleanup on the error path. |\n114|| writeCustodyFile | StagedFile.Sync | enroll.go 180:12 | no | Credential fsync before the atomic rename. |\n115|| writeCustodyFile | FileSystem.Rename | enroll.go 188:12 | no | Atomic install of the credential file. |\n116|| writeCustodyFile | FileSystem.Lstat | enroll.go 191:15 | no | Post-install existence probe. |\n117|| (EnrollmentMaterial).Format | fmt.State.Write | export.go 27:9 | no | Redacted `%v` formatting; no filesystem I/O. |\n118|| (Store).JointCommit | FileSystem.Lstat | joint.go 254:15 | no | Committed-state probe inside the joint commit. |\n119|| compensateLocked | FileSystem.ReadFile | joint.go 356:24, 365:20 | no | Marker/config reads during in-hold compensation. |\n120|| markerPresent | FileSystem.Lstat | joint.go 532:12 | no | Pending-commit marker existence probe. |\n121|| readCompensationMarker | FileSystem.Lstat | joint.go 401:19 | no | Marker probe before the compensation read. |\n122|| readCompensationMarker | FileSystem.ReadFile | joint.go 411:19 | no | Owner-only marker read. |\n123|| recoverLocked | FileSystem.Lstat | joint.go 467:15, 473:15 | no | Marker/trust probes during recovery. |\n124|| recoverLocked | FileSystem.ReadFile | joint.go 480:19, 493:24 | no | Marker/trust reads during recovery. |\n125|| removeMarkerLocked | FileSystem.Remove | joint.go 580:12 | no | Marker removal under the exclusive hold. |\n126|| resolveFailedReplace | FileSystem.ReadFile | joint.go 301:24 | no | Post-failure configuration read for pin verification. |\n127|| openLock | FileSystem.Lstat | lock_unix.go 41:12, 68:15 | no | Lock-file probes during atomic lock init. |\n128|| openLock | FileSystem.CreateExclusive | lock_unix.go 51:12 | no | Non-replacing exclusive lock-file creation. |\n129|| openLock | FileSystem.Chmod | lock_unix.go 62:12 | no | Owner-only mode enforcement on the lock file. |\n130|| checkP256Point | elliptic.Curve.IsOnCurve | profile_checks.go 45:6 | no | P-256 point validation; no I/O. |\n131|| (Store).Initialize | FileSystem.Lstat | transact.go 168:15 | no | Store existence probe during initialize. |\n132|| cleanupStagedFile | FileSystem.Remove | transact.go 313:7 | no | Staged-file cleanup on the failure path. |\n133|| commitDocument | FileSystem.CreateTemp | transact.go 276:17 | yes | Staged trust-document creation. |\n134|| commitDocument | StagedFile.Name | transact.go 280:10 | yes | Staged trust name for the atomic rename. |\n135|| commitDocument | StagedFile.Sync | transact.go 286:12 | yes | Trust-document fsync before the atomic rename. |\n136|| commitDocument | StagedFile.Close | transact.go 287:7, 290:12 | yes | Staged handle close on error and success paths. |\n137|| commitDocument | FileSystem.Chmod | transact.go 293:12 | yes | Owner-only mode enforcement on the staged trust. |\n138|| commitDocument | FileSystem.Rename | transact.go 301:12 | yes | Atomic publish of the trust document. |\n139|| loadCommitted | FileSystem.Lstat | transact.go 246:15 | no | Committed-trust probe. |\n140|| loadCommitted | FileSystem.ReadFile | transact.go 256:19 | no | Owner-only committed-trust read. |\n141|| readSnapshotLocked | FileSystem.Lstat | transact.go 133:15 | no | Snapshot-file probe. |\n142|| readSnapshotLocked | FileSystem.ReadFile | transact.go 143:19 | no | Owner-only snapshot read. |\n143|| syncDir | FileSystem.OpenDirectory | transact.go 332:17 | no | Open the store directory for the post-commit fsync. |\n144|| syncDir | SyncedDirectory.Sync | transact.go 336:12 | no | Directory fsync that makes the commit durable. |\n145|| syncDir | SyncedDirectory.Close | transact.go 337:7, 340:9 | no | Directory handle close on each outcome path. |\n146|| writeAll | interface{Write}.Write | transact.go 319:19 | no | Byte sink for staged trust content. |\n147|| (CredentialEntry).Format | fmt.State.Write | trust.go 67:9 | no | Redacted `%v` formatting; no filesystem I/O. |\n148|| (TrustStore).Format | fmt.State.Write | trust.go 62:63 | no | Redacted `%v` formatting; no filesystem I/O. |\n149|\n150|No non-callee interface method value was found in the production scan:\n151|every interface-typed selector in `internal/config` and\n152|`internal/hosttrust` production sources is the callee of an\n153|inventoried call above.\n154|\n155|## Other admitted edges\n156|\n157|Function-valued parameters and locals (`censusIndirectPolicies`):\n158|`applyV4`/`rollbackV4` `openStore` (test seam that opens the trust\n159|store), `validateRootKinds` `stat` (filesystem probe seam),\n160|`sshFlagValueRule` `permits` and `admitSSHArguments`/`admitSSHOption`\n161|`rule` (pure SSH validators), `writeTempFile` `clean` (local staging\n162|cleanup), hosttrust `fn`/`boundary`/`revalidate`/`replace`/`restore`\n163|(lock/hold/joint-commit callbacks that run inside the caller's hold),\n164|`unlock`/`unlockBootstrap`/`exclusiveUnlock` (local unlock closures),\n165|`accept` (string-decode acceptor), and `failed` (compensation\n166|outcome). Each is admitted only as the exact resolved declaration\n167|object inside its owning function.\n168|\n169|Named immutable values (`censusAllowedFunctionValues`,\n170|`censusAllowedExternalFunctionValues`): `tomlDecode`,\n171|`migrationError`, `configError`, `loaderError`,\n172|`terminalCapabilitySet`, `trustError` (error constructors and the\n173|immutable terminal set), and `elliptic.P256` (curve selector). The\n174|single immediately invoked package initializer is the\n175|`terminalCapabilitySet` construction\n176|(`censusAllowedFunctionInitializers`). Function-valued struct fields\n177|(`censusAllowedFunctionFields`): `sshOptionRule.permits` (pure SSH\n178|validator), `Inputs.LookupEnv`/`Stat`/`ReadFile` (production input\n179|seams).\n180|\n181|Filesystem backend definitions (`censusBackendMethods`): the bodies of\n182|the exact `(osFileSystem, ...)` and `(osMigrationFileSystem, ...)`\n183|method pairs implement the seams, so direct `os` calls inside them are\n184|the definition of the interface, not new write paths. A new method on\n185|a backend receiver is scanned as a new write path. Gated pair helpers\n186|(`replaceDurably`, `writeTempReplace`) may only be called inside a\n187|`JointCommit`/`WithExclusiveHold`/`WithExclusiveHoldForConfig`\n188|closure; trust/custody helpers (`commitDocument`,\n189|`commitConfigBinding`, `removeMarkerLocked`, `writeCustodyFile`,\n190|`writeTempFile`, `ensureOwnerDir`, `secureStaged`) only inside their\n191|censused writer definitions.\n192|\n193|## Negative evidence\n194|\n195|- `TestWritePathCensusRejectsUnlistedInterfaceCallSite` (committed\n196|  port of the CR11 `reviewer_callsite_test.go` probe) copies the\n197|  module, plants real `filesystem.Rename` calls before AND after\n198|  `requireHoldForConfig` in `replaceDurably`, and runs the production\n199|  census plus a valid-hold witness in a child `go test`. The child\n200|  witness must PASS (both plants rename real files through the\n201|  production entry) while the child census FAILs with a\n202|  `write-path census violation` for both unlisted sites.\n203|- `writepath-interface-callsite-skip` preserves the allowlisted\n204|  interface-method object identity while admitting the same method at\n205|  every call site and before hold verification; it propagates its\n206|  overlay into the child module and is killed by the regression above\n207|  (child exit 0 under the mutant, outer test exit 1).\n208|- `writepath-method-value-skip` preserves the raw-mutation symbol\n209|  check while admitting backend method values; killed by\n210|  `TestWritePathGateFlagsExecutableRogues/backend_method_value`.\n211|- The `TestWritePathGateFlagsExecutableRogues` suite (28 subtests:\n212|  direct/package-var/alias/returned-closure controls, aliased and\n213|  dot-imported writers, map/slice/struct-field/parameter function\n214|  values, promoted embedded methods, backend receiver/method-value\n215|  rogues, interface/generic/type-parameter/channel/IIFE shapes, and\n216|  real-file witnesses) plus\n217|  `TestWritePathCensusFailsClosedOnUnresolvedCallee` and the five\n218|  `TestWritePathGateFlagsUnlockedCaller` controls all pass; the\n219|  reviewer's 17 standalone census plants are retained as killed.\n220|- Full batteries (below) run the behavioral package suites, not only\n221|  the static checker.\n222|\n223|## Production call-site map\n224|\n225|| Boundary | Production call site | Negative production evidence |\n226||---|---|---|\n227|| Config4/legacy pair writers | `config.Migrate`, `PreviewV4`, `ApplyV4`, `RollbackV4`, `writeTempReplace`, `replaceDurably` | zero/released/foreign/wrong-path/symlink/foreign-root and stale-source tests |\n228|| Pair resolution | `config.Load`/`ResolvePaths` → `localstore.ResolvePaths` | invalid class/context, empty override, platform-default and environment-bound tests |\n229|| Trust store custody | `hosttrust.Open`, `ValidateCustody`, `Store.Initialize` | missing, malformed, unsafe mode, wrong kind, unreadable and binding tests |\n230|| Exclusive pair hold | `WithExclusiveHoldForConfig`, `HeldExclusive.ValidateConfigPaths` | zero/released/foreign pair and foreign-state-root tests |\n231|| Joint durable commit | `hosttrust.Store.JointCommit`, `Recover`, `convergeLocked` | marker tamper, source/replacement divergence, compensation and crash tests |\n232|| Authorization generation | `AuthorizeDispatch`, `WithMutationAuthorization` | stale older/newer, revocation and intervention tests |\n233|\n234|The source audit records exactly one non-test\n235|`localstore.ResolvePaths` call in `internal/config/loader.go`; no\n236|legacy free-string config/state tuple signatures remain in\n237|`internal/`.","final_result":true}}}
