{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c661","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ada8-0185-76f0-8192-f6e1be48611d"},"sequence":395,"recorded_at":1780531400000785,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e58530cc-c434-4c84-a6d6-35c15a8ccfca","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"e58530cc-c434-4c84-a6d6-35c15a8ccfca","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e58530cc-c434-4c84-a6d6-35c15a8ccfca"},"call_id":"call_01a0ada8a60e77b785f7f5a2de5f265c","text":"Read text file `/tmp/rev12/TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev12.md`.\n1|# TASK-260909-2ez769 — typed write-path census rev12\n2|\n3|## Gate\n4|\n5|The production mutation boundary is audited by\n6|`internal/config/writepath_census_types_test.go` through\n7|`TestWritePathCensusGate` (`censusViolations` dispatches to\n8|`censusTypedViolations`; the syntax walker in `writepath_census_test.go`\n9|is a historical reference only). The census loads the active Go build\n10|context with `golang.org/x/tools/go/packages`, resolves calls through\n11|`go/types`, and fails closed for unresolved calls, non-`*types.Func`\n12|targets, unlisted object identities, and unlisted call sites.\n13|\n14|An interface or type-parameter edge is admitted only when all three\n15|hold: (1) the resolved `*types.Func` selection object is the exact\n16|inventoried method object for the enclosing declaration (package path,\n17|receiver, method); (2) the call's source file/line/column equals an\n18|inventoried site for that method in that declaration; (3) for the four\n19|pair-writer declarations, a top-level fail-fast hold guard\n20|(`requireHold`/`requireHoldForConfig`/`requireHoldForRoot` in an\n21|`if`-with-`return` statement, no `else`) lexically precedes the\n22|statement containing the call. A new call, a moved call, or an escaped\n23|method value of an already-used interface method is a new edge and is\n24|refused until it is reviewed into the inventory. Method spelling alone\n25|never admits an interface edge.\n26|\n27|Name-keyed maps (`censusOSMutations`, `censusRawMutations`,\n28|`censusPairHelpers`, `censusTrustHelpers`, `censusCustodyHelpers`,\n29|`censusGatedIdents`, `censusBackendMethods`) are used only for\n30|fail-closed DETECTION of concrete, statically resolved calls and for\n31|routing them to definition-identity checks\n32|(`censusAllowedDefinition`: same package path, same declaration name,\n33|same receiver); the former `censusIsMutationFunctionName`-style\n34|interface admission predicate is removed. Concretely: `os.Rename`\n35|matches exactly the `os`-package symbol; a method named `Rename` on\n36|any other receiver is flagged unless the enclosing declaration is the\n37|censused writer for that receiver. No name-keyed map admits an\n38|interface or type-parameter edge.\n39|\n40|Scope bound: this census executes for the active Go build context.\n41|Windows custody has native build-tagged tests and cross-compilation\n42|evidence, but no Windows runtime census execution is claimed.\n43|\n44|## Admitted interface call sites (119 sites, 90 groups)\n45|\n46|`HOLD` marks the four pair-writer declarations whose admitted sites\n47|must additionally be dominated by the top-level hold guard. Positions\n48|are `file:line:column` of the call expression in the rev12 candidate.\n49|\n50|### internal/config\n51|\n52|| Function | Edge | Sites | Hold | Production justification |\n53||---|---|---|---|---|\n54|| Load | io/fs.FileInfo.Mode | loader.go 260:6 | no | Mode check on the loaded configuration file metadata. |\n55|| loadAbsentConfig | io/fs.FileInfo.IsDir | loader.go 326:6 | no | Directory probe while synthesizing an absent configuration. |\n56|| validateRootKinds | io/fs.FileInfo.IsDir | loader.go 518:7 | no | Root-kind directory validation for configured roots. |\n57|| replaceDurably | migrationFileSystem.Stat | migration.go 406:15, 423:20 | yes | Pre/post-replace existence and identity stats for the atomic swap. |\n58|| replaceDurably | io/fs.FileInfo.Mode | migration.go 410:6, 424:78, 438:100, 450:104 | yes | Mode checks on the files being replaced and staged. |\n59|| replaceDurably | migrationFileSystem.Link | migration.go 417:12 | yes | Hard-link backup step of the durable replacement. |\n60|| replaceDurably | migrationFileSystem.ReadFile | migration.go 422:24 | yes | Byte read used to verify staged content before the final rename. |\n61|| replaceDurably | migrationFileSystem.Remove | migration.go 419:8, 425:8, 429:12, 443:7, 459:9 | yes | Cleanup of staging/rollback temporaries on each outcome path. |\n62|| replaceDurably | migrationFileSystem.Rename | migration.go 442:12, 452:18 | yes | Atomic staging rename and final replacement rename. |\n63|| syncDirectory | migrationFileSystem.OpenDirectory | migration.go 509:17 | no | Open the configuration directory for the post-replace fsync. |\n64|| syncDirectory | migrationDirectory.Sync | migration.go 513:12 | no | Directory fsync that makes the rename durable. |\n65|| syncDirectory | migrationDirectory.Close | migration.go 514:7, 517:9 | no | Directory handle close on success and error paths. |\n66|| writeAll | io.Writer.Write | migration.go 496:19 | no | Byte sink for staged configuration content. |\n67|| writeTempFile | migrationFileSystem.CreateTemp | migration.go 468:15 | no | Owner-only staged temporary file creation. |\n68|| writeTempFile | migrationFile.Name | migration.go 472:9 | no | Staged file name for the subsequent atomic rename. |\n69|| writeTempFile | migrationFile.Close | migration.go 474:7, 487:12 | no | Staged handle close on error and success paths. |\n70|| writeTempFile | migrationFileSystem.Remove | migration.go 475:7, 488:7 | no | Staged temporary cleanup on error paths. |\n71|| writeTempFile | migrationFile.Chmod | migration.go 478:12 | no | Owner-only mode enforcement on the staged file. |\n72|| writeTempFile | migrationFile.Sync | migration.go 484:12 | no | File fsync before the atomic r