{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dc89","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ada8-0185-76f0-8192-f6e1be48611d"},"sequence":3231,"recorded_at":1780531400006457,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e58530cc-c434-4c84-a6d6-35c15a8ccfca","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"e58530cc-c434-4c84-a6d6-35c15a8ccfca","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e58530cc-c434-4c84-a6d6-35c15a8ccfca"},"terminal":"completed","text":"CR-12 accepted. Task TASK-260909-2ez769 is now `integrating`.\n\n**Verdict: accepted** — both CR11 findings repaired with committed regressions and independent probe confirmation:\n\n- **F1 (call-site admission):** the committed regression (CR11 plant, extended pre+post hold) passes; 5/5 of my own plants (later-position call, method-value escape, deferred call, `if false` branch, goto) refused with census exit 1. A line-preserving goto to an inventoried site is admitted by the census but behaviorally inert — all four HOLD writers guard-first, zero-hold witness still refused — recorded as a P3 observation. Narrowing mutant killed 2/2.\n- **F2 (refused rebind):** committed trio green; my own probes (target-side crash injection, stranded-index refused at Open, bound-elsewhere refusal) all pass with both associations intact.\n- **Mutation batteries on exact final source:** config 13 killed + neutral, hosttrust 34 killed + neutral, 0 survivors; 3 reviewer-owned narrowing mutants on unmutated arms (version downgrade, format leak, exclusion skip) each killed 2/2 by the expected tests.\n- **Suites/hygiene:** `go test ./...` exit 0, `-race` on config+hosttrust green, vet (native+windows) clean, gofmt/tidy clean, 4-platform builds green, 26/26 validation gates green, 74 changed paths restricted to candidate scope, worktree left uncommitted at base `5e54874`.\n- **AC:** 19 of 21 rows driven; rows 15 (Windows ACL runtime) and 21 (downstream replication) remain stated bounds.\n\nMethodology note for the record: `go -overlay` silently ignores symlink-resolved (`/private/tmp`) keys, which initially produced false mutant survivors in my `/tmp` scratch area; rerunning from a symlink-free copy reproduced every producer kill. Evidence attached as `TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev12.md` + `TASK-260909-2ez769_review-evidence-rev12.tar.gz` (verified real gzip, round-trip checked). No product edits, commits, or integration by this reviewer; live worktree untouched.","reason":null}}
